legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:3:Patterns destructure one level in explicit `match` arms and irrefutable destructuring `let`:
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:22:**PAT-1@2.** A struct or enum pattern in a `match` or an irrefutable destructuring `let` may bind a field under another name with `field: binder`, and the formatter keeps the label.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:33:**Rationale.** Renaming avoids shadowing under SCOPE-1; OD52 removes conditional and refutable destructuring sugar without changing field labels.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:290:**PAT-5@4.** A destructuring `let` consumes its scrutinee, names every field with ignored fields explicitly marked by eligible wildcards, and has an irrefutable pattern, while refutable destructuring and `let ... else` are refused and use `match` instead.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:301:**Rationale.** OD52 and OD85 require an explicit match for refutable destructuring; OD25 requires all fields, with eligible ignored fields marked explicitly.
