legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:414:**PAT-8@2.** C-style `for` headers, including destructuring initializers, are refused; a counted loop binds its immutable index only in its body.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:486:### PAT-10. Irrefutable enum destructuring matches the rest of its block
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:488:**PAT-10@2.** An irrefutable enum destructuring `let P = e;` means a one-arm `match` over the rest of its block, with binders visible only there, while a refutable pattern or `let ... else` is refused.
legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md:499:**Rationale.** OD52 removes the fallback form; an irrefutable one-arm match preserves binder scope and explicit consumption.
